From 6ce1c29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:12:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Import: the bank's Quicken or QuickBooks file (OFX, QFX,
 QBO), no columns to check

What the person sees (owner's request 2026-11-11: connect accounts or upload statements, if
it is possible, easy and documented): most banks and card sites offer a "Quicken" (QFX) or
"QuickBooks" (QBO) download beside CSV. Import now reads it on the phone, with no PC and no
column step: "Your bank's download for Checking ending 7351 (Prairie Bank): 10 lines ... The
account number is not kept." The plan's account is picked for it and the page says why; the
same file twice adds nothing; the gap warning and "count as checked" work as for a CSV; and a
ticked box under Import also sets the account's balance to the bank's own figure (its own
button when nothing is new). Account numbers are never stored: the last 4 are shown, never
saved, and the start screen's "No bank logins or account numbers, ever" still holds.

Formulas and decisions:
- core/ofx.js, our own pure reader (no dependency, no copied code; ofxtools is GPL-3 and was
  never opened; ofx-js, MIT, Apps Attic Ltd, was the candidate and is not used). One tree for
  OFX 1.x SGML (unclosed leaves) and 2.x XML. Detection by content (OFXHEADER, <?OFX, <OFX>),
  never by the file name. Decoded by the header's CHARSET: 1252 via TextDecoder plus the
  WHATWG index-windows-1252 map for 0x80-0x9F (Node decodes "windows-1252" as ISO-8859-1).
  Dates: the first 8 digits of YYYYMMDD[HHMMSS[.XXX]][[-5:EST]], zone ignored. TRNAMT keeps
  its sign (card charges negative, the plan's convention: no flip). Entities decoded.
- Only last4 leaves the parser; a FITID built from the account number has it replaced by #;
  the import record's file name has those digits replaced by XXXX.
- prepareOfx feeds prepareRows (rules, totals, gapBefore, uncoveredDays, alsoOn); prepareImport
  sends any OFX text there. New optional transactions[].extId (the cleaned FITID; DATA_MODEL
  line, no version bump): dedupe checks it first within its account (same id = duplicate,
  another id = another line even with the same key), matches a no-id line with the same key
  one for one; lines with no id are deduped by key exactly as before.
- Account guess without the number: the account holding at least half of its lines, else the
  only account of its kind, else the one at the file's bank (FI/ORG), else the person checks.
- Balance offer: LEDGERBAL (BALAMT as of DTASOF) when newer than, or different on the same day
  from, the plan's; a card's is |BALAMT| owed with the stored sign kept (saveBalance), the old
  figure kept as a point (keepOnFile), a guess on it dropped.
- The picker's accept is broad (.csv,.txt,.tsv,.ofx,.qfx,.qbo,text/csv,text/plain,
  application/x-ofx,application/vnd.intu.qfx); the content decides.
- docs/RESOURCES.md: Plaid's free Development tier ended 2024-06-20 (a Trial of 10 logins is
  left; not planned); ofx-js is github.com/bradenmacdonald/ofx-js. transactions/connect's
  purpose (module.js, README, catalog) drops "or Plaid". Import README: status line and an OFX
  section; catalog row and module purpose name the Quicken / QuickBooks file.

view.js touched: modules/transactions/import/view.js (file read as bytes and decoded, the broad
accept list, hero and paste wording, the OFX preview: file account line, why the account was
picked, several accounts select, balance tick box or button, tiles and sample rows).

